      "children": [
        {
          "name": "heading",
          "props": {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "How a brief becomes a document"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "paragraph",
          "props": {
            "text": "The same free-canvas composition as `visual-infographic.docx.json`, drawn natively. With `renderMode: \"native\"` and the `office-open` renderer, the canvas becomes one Word drawing group: the chevrons are real shapes and the labels are real text, so the words below are selectable, searchable and editable in Word — and nothing is rasterized, so this example renders with no LibreOffice, no poppler and no rasterization service."
          }
        },
        {
